window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>The fire’s gone. The dead stayed behind.</b></p> <p>Ethan Matthews thought coming back to Crestwood High would bring closure. He’s not a student anymore. Now he’s a teacher. And he’s married to Hanna, his high school sweetheart, one of the few who survived the fire that scarred them both.</p> <p>But something’s still lurking in those halls. Whispers echo through empty classrooms. Shadows shift when no one’s there. The ones who died? They never left. And they’re not here to haunt Ethan. They’re trying to make him remember.</p> <p>As old memories crawl back, Ethan starts questioning everything he thought he knew. The deeper he digs, the darker it gets. And the more he wonders if he’s been living a lie.</p> <p><b>Some memories are locked away for a reason.</b><br> <b><br> But at Crestwood High, nothing stays buried forever.</b></p>"; 
